# Localization work queue (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-08-17): **as we add and change things,
they become recorded in the localization repo as new work.**

There is no separate localization GitHub repository. **`core-assets` is
the localization home.** The durable to-do list is
`core-assets/content/localization-work/`.

## The rule

> **When an agent adds or changes operator-visible Help, manuals, or
> other must-localize strings, it records a work item in
> `core-assets/content/localization-work/` in the same change set.
> Translators read that queue. Agent draft catalogs do not close an
> item. Closing requires reviewed catalogs for every required tag.**

## When this applies

Record (or reopen) a queue item when any of the following lands:

- A new Help chapter, operator manual, or auditor / admin / user guide
- A change to English source prose that already has a queue row
- New must-localize chrome on reports, binder, risks, legal notices,
  IR, dashboards, or other rows in
  [`compliance-artifacts-must-localize.mdc`](compliance-artifacts-must-localize.mdc)

Does **not** apply to internal `docs/dev` runbooks, Cursor rules, or
lab scripts that never ship to an operator.

## How to record

From the `core-assets` repo root (Python 3, stdlib only):

```text
python3 scripts/localization-work/localization_work.py add --id <stable.id> --title "..." --source-path <path> --source-file <local-file>
python3 scripts/localization-work/localization_work.py record --id <stable.id> --source-file <local-file>
```

Also add a row to `content/localization-work/surfaces.json` so
`record-all` can rehash the English source later.

`record` / `record-all` reopen the item when the source SHA-256 changes.

## Closing

Set `status` to `closed` only when every `required_tags` entry has a
reviewed catalog. Draft `de` / `fr` / `es` strings are **not** close.
Missing Tier 1 tags (`en-GB`, `zh-Hans` today) keep the item **open**.
Closing is not a Met or certified claim
([`compliance-claims-honesty.mdc`](compliance-claims-honesty.mdc)).

## Forbidden

- Shipping a new Help chapter or must-localize surface without a queue
  row in the same change set
- Treating agent-written locale JSON as closed localization work
- Adding a git hook or product environment variable for this queue
- Lab hostnames, lab accounts, or agent thinking in queue notes
- Inventing a second localization GitHub repo for the to-do list

## Required agent behavior

1. Enqueue or `record` in `core-assets` in the **same change set** as
   the English source change.
2. Mirror this rule to `core-assets/.cursor/rules/` when editing the
   workspace copy ([`auto-commit-push.mdc`](auto-commit-push.mdc)).
3. Point translators at `content/localization-work/queue.md`.

